Landowner hunting tags-amendments. 25LSO-0576, 1.0
FISCAL NOTE
The fiscal impact is indeterminable.
In addition to expenditures for computer programming modifications, the Game and
Fish Department (Game and Fish) estimates the cost to record the sale and reissuance
of each landowner license is $39.00. For reference, Game and Fish reported 3,507
landowner licenses were issued in 2024. Because the quantity of landowner licenses
that would be sold and potential increases in landowner license applications is
unknown, the fiscal impact of this legislation is indeterminable.
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
NON-ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT
Anticipated Expenditure increase
HIGHWAY FUND $3,657 $0 $0
Source of expenditure increase:
Computer programming to accommodate the sale and reissuance of landowner hunting
licenses.
Assumptions:
Approximately 60 hours of computer programming at $60.95 per hour.
All attributes of the original license, including residency, remain in effect.
The cost to record the sale and reissuance of a landowner license is $39.00.
The expenditure increase reflected above could be considered an administrative
cost. However, for simplicity and to follow consistent practice on legislation of
this type, it is included on the fiscal note.
